{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich","id":1550973,"title":"Is it possible to be a \"moral\" Tremere Lich?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-12T15:42:34-07:00","id":1550973,"title":"Is it possible to be a \"moral\" Tremere Lich?","content":"Yeah, I know the idea of being moral while also being Tremere is an oxymoron, but I'm still curious. Say a lich wanted to be a horrible soul-eater, either to prove a point, or if they had once been a member of the Tremere before going rogue and no longer want to eat souls. What would their options be? Obviously, they can't stop being a lich, and they still would need to 'gnaw' on souls at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T16:15:04-07:00","id":1550974,"title":"","content":"They could consume souls until they reach Integrity/Wisdom 1, then put them back in their vessels so they can recover. It would still leave a trail of people endangered and deeply traumatized by soul loss, plus with a long process to recover their sense of self, but they technically wouldn't destroy any souls.<br /> <br /> Another option would be to do the same in exchange for Awakened souls. They have invaluable tomes on an Abyssal Invader, or a potent Grimmoire, maybe a map to a new ruin. These can be rented with the soul of a guarantor being used for payments.<br /> <br /> They could try to buy them off a Seer of Mammon. If everything is for sale, surely they just need to find the correct vendor, right ?<br /> <br /> They could hunt Scelesti, Rapt and Banishers, since they normally are seen as major threats. But they would need to be very good trackers and constantly face really dangerous foes.<br /> <br /> Since Fetches have pieces of a Changeling's soul, they could offer their services to the local Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T16:35:36-07:00","id":1550975,"title":"","content":"I always had the doubt of consumables and time travel.<br /> <br /> If you are a lich, eat a soul, and then travel back 1 scene with &quot;Shifting Sands&quot;, you should keep the benefits of having consumed the soul... The same way that you would get the drawback of being shot for example.<br /> <br /> What is stopping any soul reaper from doing this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T16:39:50-07:00","id":1550976,"title":"","content":"Strictly speaking, a Tremere can get by on either no souls or one soul with a living original owner, provided they take no other damage and are alright with having no Willpower dots (or needing to buy new Willpower dots for other purposes on a regular basis); the resistant aggravated damage heals at the same rate it's inflicted as long as there isn't newer damage taking priority.<br /> <br /> The koimaomai in turn provides a means of reducing the hunger (and thereby extending the timer) by reducing their Hollow rating, but that's risky and requires some long-term planning. to avoid becoming a preta.<br /> <br /> There's a tilt on the classic Nosferatu grift of feeding on sleeping people: a Tremere who can get ahold of souls from comatose people has a relatively consequence-free use of the Soul Starvation buffer roll, provided they're not worried about someone pulling the plug or waking up their discount thralls.<br /> <br /> Immortality is likely to have its due in the absence of an elaborate machine to feed this uncharacteristically repentant member of the most entitled mages in the world (who may, in their contrition, see their former peers convinced that if they aren't keeping up with the Sevenfold Oath they're fair game), but puttering along with no unused souls left is about as feasible as running a Mummy game where the Arisen wake up during a Sothic Turn, make Descent rolls until they reach Sekhem 1, and then avoid dying or blaspheming against the Judges for the next several decades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T23:37:18-07:00","id":1550984,"title":"","content":"If you have a soul in reserve (say, by casting Soul Jar on someone who's about to die (from causes unrelated to you, if you want to be moral about it)) then you can actually just swap souls around with people without letting anyone suffer from soulloss, as long as you don't use them up completely.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's supposed to be completely harmless to swap out someone's soul, but ruleswise they're completely plug'n'play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T07:04:47-07:00","id":1550990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1550974#post1550974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could consume souls until they reach Integrity/Wisdom 1, then put them back in their vessels so they can recover. It would still leave a trail of people endangered and deeply traumatized by soul loss, plus with a long process to recover their sense of self, but they technically wouldn't destroy any souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a thought; if the Tremere have a concern with secrecy and have managed to apparently keep the scope of their operation effectively under wraps for a thousand years, why would they want to leave behind trails of people showing signs of soul loss?<br /> <br /> Here's another thought; if, at a certain low level of advancement, they can remove and attach souls basically at will, why ever wait until the soul they carry is totally depleted before getting a new one?<br /> <br /> It was my understanding that, by and large, the Tremere make a point of replacing the souls they take with the souls that they're currently holding.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are times that they carry a number of souls in reserve, in which case they probably don't have any to spare. But like... you don't need to do that all the time (indeed, you probably can't), so the extent of people you leave behind soulless can be effectively minimised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T07:27:11-07:00","id":1550991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1550975#post1550975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always had the doubt of consumables and time travel.<br /> <br /> If you are a lich, eat a soul, and then travel back 1 scene with &quot;Shifting Sands&quot;, you should keep the benefits of having consumed the soul... The same way that you would get the drawback of being shot for example.<br /> <br /> What is stopping any soul reaper from doing this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere aren't literally eating souls in the sense of popping them in their mouth, chewing them up and digesting them, and converting the result into nutrition. Their Gnosis is transformed into a form of spiritual hunger that degrades souls that have been attached to them and, in the absence of such, eats away at the Tremere's own pattern. At most levels of this Gnosis substitute, called Hollow, it takes months for this degradation to occur. Even in lacking a soul, it takes months to actually be killed by it.<br /> <br /> So if you're soulless when you go back in time, you're still soulless for the same reasons that you'll still have an injury, and still be subject to the condition that causes Tremere to lose Willpower and then take resistant aggravated damage for every week that they go without a soul.<br /> <br /> Actually, looking at it now, a soul attached to a Tremere is only actually destroyed if it is expelled to be free floating after having been used up past the point of being nourishing. The soul continues to exist for as long as it remains attached to the Tremere, and can be transmitted to another soulless person directly if desired.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that when Tremere use their innate powers to remove a soul, it doesn't automatically become attached to them. This is why it's perfectly possible for them to use a soul past the point of it being nourishing, keep it around until they find a suitable replacement, pull that out of the original owner, expel the depleted one directly into the newly soulless person, and then attach the fresh soul to themselves.<br /> <br /> (Also, keep in mind that in the current lexicon, &quot;lich&quot; is the term for an immortal mage. &quot;Reaper&quot; refers to those who steal and harness souls.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T07:41:16-07:00","id":1550992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1550984#post1550984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's supposed to be completely harmless to swap out someone's soul, but ruleswise they're completely plug'n'play.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're actually given the rules for what happens when a person receives a soul that is no longer nourishing to the Tremere; they gain the Soul Shocked Condition, and lose a dot of permanent Willpower.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that, typically, the worst that happens from being given a soul that a Tremere fully used up is that you feel emotionally drained to a greater or lesser extent (you roll your current Willpower points as a dice pool and only keep one per success), and can't reclaim Willpower from Anchors until you've gained full Willpower recovery from other sources.<br /> <br /> Depending on the person in question (and presuming they're in ignorance of how to deliberately resolve the Condition), that's an experience of not feeling the gratification and affirmation of some essential parts of your character that goes away after a few days of good bedrest, or keeps getting a bit drawn out because they keep having to exert themselves highly in intense situations.<br /> <br /> It's probably affecting to not feel Willpower recovery as a result of things like Virtue and Vice for people who can't contextualize it, but not totally devastating.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T08:32:53-07:00","id":1550996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1550992#post1550992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're actually given the rules for what happens when a person receives a soul that is no longer nourishing to the Tremere; they gain the Soul Shocked Condition, and lose a dot of permanent Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's souls that are fully drained, that would simply disintegrate if expelled. A half-nibbled soul doesn't have any explicit rules for reintegration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T22:14:58-07:00","id":1551011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1550996#post1550996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's souls that are fully drained, that would simply disintegrate if expelled. A half-nibbled soul doesn't have any explicit rules for reintegration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the way that Dave and Malcolm have talked about it, being plug and play by the rules is absolutely meant to represent an idea that exchanging one soul for another is simple and clean.<br /> <br /> Hence the temptation of what to do if you have somebody that needs a soul.<br /> <br /> It's like the fiction piece in the compilation with the Nemean. He brings Khonsu back to life and gives him the soul of some guy he basically murdered, and Khonsu is just fine and it's messed up how easy that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T05:38:20-07:00","id":1551037,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to me how the original proposition is based on the idea of somebody who has replaced their Gnosis with Hollow who wants to basically abandon the Order for the sake of morality. Because the thing I've been hinting at with most of my posts is that I think it's perfectly cromulent to be a Tremere who remains part of the Order, and even lives by the Sevenfold Oath, and be moral enough.<br /> <br /> Like, I honestly think it's easier for them to get by with relatively little harm on souls then it is for the literal vampires who need blood, given the whole &quot;you can replace the soul you take&quot; deal. Once you have that, it's just a question of how you choose to go about your journey of investigating the nature and power of the soul, and it's possible to do that without even removing or damaging them.<br /> <br /> Now sure, by and large Tremere probably are conducting their investigations in a manner that causes some degree of harm, whether in the experiments and observations themselves or how they'll deal with threats and obstacles to their work. The Order has a culture that emphasizes a certain ruthlessness in their conduct towards anybody who is not themselves (and even a kind of mercenary attitude internally), but even that has more nuance to it than just going around leaving behind trails of people suffering without their souls, and you can still have a plausible character who is within the Order and even committed to its beliefs and ideals who still doesn't really gel with that side of their culture. <br /> <br /> Plus, there's that whole thing where the Oath outright demands that they destroy everything else that steals souls. You can arguably make a good look for yourself by dedicated pursuit of other Reapers and varied monsters that might be less gentle with the soul than even Tremere are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T13:09:06-07:00","id":1551049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1550974#post1550974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could consume souls until they reach Integrity/Wisdom 1, then put them back in their vessels so they can recover. It would still leave a trail of people endangered and deeply traumatized by soul loss, plus with a long process to recover their sense of self, but they technically wouldn't destroy any souls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes me think of Dumb and Dumber when Lloyd and Harry hand over the suitcase full of ransom money that's been exchanged for IOUs.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to do this falls under the &quot;road to hell is paved with good intentions,&quot; idea. Part of them wanted to do what they thought was right, but things are just going to get increasingly worse the longer they're out there trying to think they're being moral in the first place.<br /> <br /> Traditionally in Chronicles and World of Darkness the &quot;moral&quot; take on predation has involved victimizing those a character sees as deserving of becoming a victim. &quot;He only drains blood from criminals,&quot; kind of mindset, though who's deserving of that can vary wildly depending on the character's circumstances, culture, and upbringing.<br /> <br /> The end result is not going to be a shining and objective paragon of morality, but a twisted monster potentially worse than other Tremere, insisting they're doing something good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T14:30:56-07:00","id":1551053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1551049#post1551049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally in Chronicles and World of Darkness the &quot;moral&quot; take on predation has involved victimizing those a character sees as deserving of becoming a victim. &quot;He only drains blood from criminals,&quot; kind of mindset, though who's deserving of that can vary wildly depending on the character's circumstances, culture, and upbringing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's not the case with Vampire: the Requiem. There the... I wouldn't even call it the &quot;moral&quot; take on feeding so much as the default one, is to target it at people where the arrangement is nominally reciprocal, but mired in an unequal power dynamic.<br /> <br /> You know, keeping in mind that it is not necessary to drain a person's blood to the point of death, and probably often more sensible not to.<br /> <br /> And as I said, the consequences of swapping souls is arguably less harmful and intrusive than a vampire feeding off of somebody. Not just in the point of &quot;this inflicts damage that moves one closer to death&quot;, but in the addictive qualities of being fed upon. Nobody feels good about having their soul removed and replaced by a Tremere, and if the mage doesn't even wait until it's drained past the point of nourishment, it won't even cause any long term harm. There aren't even any rules about how long a soul takes to become nourishing again, which might be taken to mean it's almost instantaneous once attached to a pattern without Hollow.<br /> <br /> But the point is, one could take cues from Requiem to have a Tremere who seeks at least nominal consent before swapping souls. You could even have a character who argues that the Sevenfold Oath mandates such a thing, even if the majority of the Order would disagree.<br /> <br /> Note that this still has a capacity to be exploitative even beyond the immediate consequences. A person who has their soul removed by Tremere attainments does, after all, gain a tilt that makes them feel a deep seated need to acquiesce to the demands of the Tremere.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T14:52:00-07:00","id":1551054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1551053#post1551053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the point is, one could take cues from Requiem to have a Tremere who seeks at least nominal consent before swapping souls. You could even have a character who argues that the Sevenfold Oath mandates such a thing, even if the majority of the Order would disagree.<br /> <br /> Note that this still has a capacity to be exploitative even beyond the immediate consequences. A person who has their soul removed by Tremere attainments does, after all, gain a tilt that makes them feel a deep seated need to acquiesce to the demands of the Tremere.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given how the Tremere don't respect someone who gives something away, could they instead find someone willing to rent or sell their soul, by which the Tremere would be expected to treat them with more respect instead of just yanking the soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T16:38:30-07:00","id":1551055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550973-is-it-possible-to-be-a-moral-tremere-lich?p=1551054#post1551054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how the Tremere don't respect someone who gives something away, could they instead find someone willing to rent or sell their soul, by which the Tremere would be expected to treat them with more respect instead of just yanking the soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's still seeking consent, it's just making the consent conditional.<br /> <br /> It's your idea for a character, but I think either could be in operation. The one Tremere who is concerned with consent might expect or even insist that a person demand something in exchange, and explicitly refrain unless they do so. The other Tremere might think the only conscionable way to do so is with consent that they'll accept from a person who won't opt to haggle, but still look upon that person with a level of condescension verging on contempt; the Tremere is acting in a way that they're convinced is good, but looks down upon the other party as flaunting their lack of enlightenment and the little respect that should come with that. Like the way some people engage in charitable work.<br /> <br /> I would keep in mind that the powers of Hollowing do not, to my knowledge, reference any point of being like Awakened magic and thus subject to Quiescence. A Sleeper made explicitly aware of all this is at risk of breaking points to Integrity the same way as they are when knowingly encountering anything else supernatural, but they can have it explained to them in a way they'll remember.<br /> <br /> Hell, given that it's a lot more esoteric than something like having somebody bite at a blood vessel and drain a bit, it might actually be easier to rationalise away in some fashion, especially if they never get Soul Shocked for it. This guy is talking about taking and replacing your soul, and sure when they lay hands on you it feels weird for a few moments, but that's surely just the intensity of the whole proceeding. They're a bit of an oddball with some fanciful notions, but hey, it's no harm playing along for a bit, and they are pretty compelling otherwise, so they're worth still hanging around with for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T02:44:56-07:00","id":1551150,"title":"","content":"Their 1e writeup mentions Vedmak operating like that when they were a Legacy (pre-absorption into the Tremere as a House) they'd accept souls from volunteers to power their monster-hunting. Their 2e writeup doesn't mention it, but it's focused on what they're like now, centuries of being a House later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-20T06:20:42-07:00","id":1551155,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth placing the Tremere in a context in which Second Edition as a whole seems to have opted to add more complexity and nuance to Left-Handed mages. By and large they're still doing stuff that is at odds with the values of the Pentacle Orders, and being positioned as antagonists means they're generally going to do stuff that is morally dubious at least within any given story.<br /> <br /> But there's motivation and reasoning to their actions that makes them more than something like mindlessly evil generic cultists who go around kicking puppies and stealing all the cakes. That should mean there's more variety and depth to the manner in which they investigate their particular Mysteries, even when those Mysteries do go to areas that are transgressions to most mages.<br /> <br /> Never mind that no small amount of antagonism might arise organically not from what the mage is pursuing, but what they do to try and keep it out of sight of other mages who might attack them over it.<br /> <br /> This at the same time as there's emphasis on how Obsessions that are perfectly reasonable under the Lex Magica aren't necessarily on the up and up either. It's not so crude as to be &quot;the different factions are basically indistinguishable and all terrible&quot;, but still more sophisticated than there being an unambiguous delineation between good and bad mages.<br /> <br /> So when it comes to a Tremere, I think it's worth developing what that individual wants and how they might go about getting it, with an eye to how that should have more to it than just taking as many souls as they can just because. That creates a lot of room for Tremere who conduct themselves in a more acceptable manner, but still leaves even the enemy Tremere with more variety not just in personality, but how they might be dealt with.<br /> <br /> (I actually think the Scelesti are the greatest beneficiaries of this shift. For most of First Edition, they could not have been less interesting for just being the placeholder of &quot;mage who is doing a thing because it's bad&quot;. I find the presentation in Nameless and Accursed to provide a lot more to work with in the point of thinking about what exactly a given mage might want to draw out of the Abyss or harness the symbolism of their altered Paths for or do with greater power over Paradox. Even for the couple examples that are straight up evil cultists, they're more interesting for what they get in context, motive and methodology, and the actual nature of that part of the Abyss they've become enamoured with.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}